  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining Electoral Engagement for Democracy (SEED)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  WIth FY 2022 funds this activity will:Build the capacity of civil society organizations (CSOs) to conduct domestic election monitoring and voter education, focused on election results, electoral violence, and access to electoral processes for marginalized groups including  women, youth, persons with disabilities, and internally displaced persons. Support the recruitment and training of domestic monitors that will conduct traditional observation and deploy parallel vote tabulations for off-cycle elections. Through these interventions, USAID will strengthen  the technical, organizational, and political support of key organizations actively engaged in Nigeria&apos;s electoral system to help produce credible outcomes and long-term sustainability of electoral processes in Nigeria. More credible electoral and political processes contribute to strengthening good governance in Nigeria, which is a key priority of the Integrated Country Strategy for Nigeria, the USAID CDCS, and directly supports Goal 4 of the 2022-20226 Joint Strategic Plan..</narrative>
  </description>
